{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>And Jacob dwelt in the land of his father's sojournings</b> — For he says that the chieftains of Esau dwelt in the land of their possession, that is to say, the land that they acquired for themselves as an everlasting possession, but Jacob dwelt as a sojourner, like his father, in a land not theirs but rather Canaan's. The intent is to declare that they choose to sojourn in the chosen land, and that there was fulfilled in them \"for your seed shall be a sojourner in a land not theirs\" (Genesis 15:13), and not in Esau, for in Jacob alone are they called \"your seed.\""], :book :genesis, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 37, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T03:40:41.589827185Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}